Patch 0003 of the ztOS camera-application candidates. Target:
ztmetro/camera/ztcamera.c at ztOS
94b35c2a1f4ceb568bc0ab60f5a1acebe7cfefaf, the pinned upstream revision.

Base: source sha256
5647a698e1db38b0af0c911a3ad2a0df1576c69bd9dbab3a6d7645dbcb17ebee (result of
0002).
Result: source sha256
4636d552fcd90000602513b8a520c9f746226f82e84635a4c94fd0ef269ed71d.

Apply after 0001, from the ztOS checkout's `ztmetro/` directory, with GNU
`patch` (the diff paths are relative to that directory, as in the local camera
kit); the header above is skipped by patch:

    cd ztmetro
    patch -p1 -F0 < ../patches/userspace/ztcamera/0003-af-settle-boost.patch

Effect: raises the AF settle from 110 ms to 170 ms (more than two 15 fps
frames), waits 280 ms at every position of a dark boosted sweep, clears the
held flag after a boost, logs cancelled sweeps and raises the sweep timeout to
9000 ms. Needs the `af_boost` code of the accepted line: it does not apply to
the camera-v3 720p30 line (4 of 10 hunks fail there), and no build of that line
contains it.

Status: candidate, not accepted state. Host-verified: applies to the published
chain without fuzz and reproduces the source hash above; the AF candidate build
and the vblank + AF build were each built twice byte-identically and passed the
artifact check host-side. Optical AF criteria were never measured: no candidate
has been run on the phone.

Derivative of a GPL-2.0-or-later upstream file, distributed under the "or
later" option; upstream copyright stays with the ztOS authors.
